SUMMARY:2026 Orange Shirt Day and the National Day for Truth and Reconciliation
DESCRIPTION:Wednesday\, September 30 is Orange Shirt Day and the National Day for Truth and Reconciliation. Here are some ways to commemorate the day:  \n\nStart or continue your journey toward reconciliation by engaging with U of T Engineering’s Indigenous Cultural Competency Toolkit.\nDownload and use a U of T Engineering virtual background or the U of T virtual background in your online meetings.\nLearn about the significance of Orange Shirt Day and wear an orange shirt on September 30.\nRead U of T’s inclusive employer guide to learn about what you can do in the workplace to create awareness among your own team.\nAttend (either in-person at Hart House or virtually) U of T’s event in honour of Orange Shirt Day and the National Day of Truth and Reconciliation on September 30.\nAttend the All-Nations Powwow at UTM on October 3.\nAttend the Barriers to Reconciliation: Walking the Path of Indigenous Allyship workshop on October 8.
URL:https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/2026-orange-shirt-day-and-the-national-day-for-truth-and-reconciliation/
END:VEVENT
