SUMMARY:Global Experiences Week 2026
DESCRIPTION:Are you looking for ways to incorporate global and international experiences in your undergraduate Engineering studies? Global Experiences Week is happening from October 13 to 15! \nLearn about global courses\, certificate and minor programs\, study and research abroad opportunities\, and work experiences abroad by attending the events and sessions scheduled throughout the week. Join us to learn about all the exciting global opportunities available to undergraduate engineering students! \n  \n\n\n\n\n	Date & TimeEventLocationRegistration\n\n\n\n\n	Tuesday\, October 13th\, 2026\n\n6:00 p.m. to 7:30 p.m.\nInternational PEY Co-op Work Terms: A Student Panel Discussion\n\nAs part of Global Experiences Week\, connect with your PEY Co-op network to obtain insights from panel speakers who have recently completed a PEY Co-op work term abroad. In this student panel discussion\, your peers will share information about their international work experiences\, and how to apply your own goals and job search strategy internationally. \n\nRefreshments will be provided.GB202\nGalbraith Building\, Room 202\n\n35 St. George St.\, 2nd floor.\n\nRegister Here\n\n\n	Wednesday\, October 14th\, 2026\n\n1:30 p.m. to 3:30 p.m.\nEngineering Global Experience Expo\n\nLooking to enhance your global fluency and your undergraduate Engineering experience? Learn about the different courses\, certificate programs\, study and research abroad opportunities\, and student organizations you can get involved with by attending the Global Education Expo! \n\nRepresentatives from departments and organizations across U of T will be present\, including the Centre for Global Engineering\, Centre for International Experience\, Summer Abroad\, Reach Alliance\, and more! Bahen Atrium\n\n40 St. George St.\, 2nd floor.\n\nRegistration is not required.\n\nDrop in anytime between 1:30 p.m. to 3:30 p.m.!\n\n\n	Thursday\, October 15th\, 2026\n\n6:00 p.m. to 7:30 p.m.\nLet's Talk Course Exchange: Information Session\n\nTo wrap up Global Experiences Week\, join this information session to hear more about course exchange at U of T Engineering! Learn how you can study abroad while staying on track with your degree\, explore partner universities\, discover funding opportunities\, and get tips on planning your application. We’ll also provide a brief overview of the Course Exchange Pathways specifically designed for Engineering undergraduate students. \n\nWhether you're curious or ready to apply\, this session will give you all the tools you need!\n\nRefreshments will be provided.GB202\nGalbraith Building\, Room 202\n\n35 St. George St.\, 2nd floor.\nRegister Here
URL:https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/global-experiences-week-2026/
CATEGORIES:Info sessions
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/sites/28/2026/09/global-experience-week.png
END:VEVENT
